{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"body":"The three conclusions in the Lean statement correspond to three separate paper statements.\n\nInspected: Read complete Lean file, including squaredDistance, characterTwist and UniformlyNonpretentious; inspected audited introduction assertions and pinned introduction equation eq:unp.\n\nEditorial revision by Codex, 26 October 2026: wording and display metadata clarified; pinned source texts and proposed relations unchanged. No human review or proof replay was added.\n\nCapture rebinding by Codex, 26 October 2026: the Atlas capture revision changed after an outside-report wording correction. The pinned Lean text, configuration, paper text and proposed relation are unchanged; no new review is implied.","content_sha256":"sha256:c5d4c35fa4e4ffa0d4129fe99e19ab550e122638357c9cebb1416fff53bb08e4","fingerprint":"sha256:76339a43c459032947b9b0fd8290c4e299b4601cd7038170490cbe462ca5fe9f","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Three configured conclusions require three paper anchors.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:e09ff958b87d795ff14b125457531f960e91c888b12b94af672c74954f406869","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.liouville_log_saving"],"explanation":"The configured Liouville theorem has one absolute positive logarithmic-saving exponent and a coefficient-dependent constant for each pair of positive-slope, nonproportional affine forms. Its sum to the natural floor of a real X matches the paper count for every real X at least three.","fingerprint":"sha256:6860844256216cd0ad679a9ab7ddf3b6f81639b8626131f168cb03e9635ba75c","limitations":"This link covers only the quantitative declaration, not the other two configured conclusions.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026#thm:q-affine","statement_sha256":"sha256:b96532053123181f525cdf71412bea773bfa47a32bf286a8cf183f800bc7bd6b"},{"declarations":["OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.binary_corrected_elliott"],"explanation":"The binary theorem treats ordinary averages of two one-bounded multiplicative functions at distinct nonnegative shifts. The inspected UniformlyNonpretentious definition quantifies over each fixed Dirichlet character and all twists of height at most the prime cutoff, matching equation eq:unp in the introduction.","fingerprint":"sha256:816193ded570fbdd795a7fa5675d438f7eefc1fec6f1a5e0c2220fd5a54da968","limitations":"Only the binary declaration is linked here; source correspondence is not proof verification.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026#thm:elliott","statement_sha256":"sha256:ba6b25091554132b4c7fedc012a703ac35b71581aa798c25155679f6f8c7a7cf"},{"declarations":["OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.affine_corrected_elliott"],"explanation":"The affine theorem has the same bounded multiplicative-function and uniform nonpretentiousness hypotheses as the corollary. Positive slopes, nonnegative intercepts and the nonzero determinant condition match, and the asserted normalized ordinary sum tends to zero.","fingerprint":"sha256:1e64332943cc8a90d49a3d09ac68fe8bce134829cb5b5ae2f1831cbf11636e47","limitations":"This is the separate affine consequence; it must not be represented by the Liouville estimate alone.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026#cor:affine","statement_sha256":"sha256:ead8fa334603b77c70c3b0016d320f86adaf1db4c1d3c9aa783646904b199245"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L20","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L64","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L81"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.liouville_log_saving","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.lean","line":43,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"e09ff958b87d795ff14b125457531f960e91c888b12b94af672c74954f406869","statement_sha256":"sha256:8b9eb7679e5cab610ce94b89b4d76bb2f02d96386d9b28ffd0cc054c1be08a03","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.lean#L43"},"text":"theorem liouville_log_saving :\n    ∃ c : ℝ, 0 < c ∧ ∀ a₁ a₂ b₁ b₂ : ℕ,\n      0 < a₁ → 0 < a₂ → a₁ * b₂ ≠ a₂ * b₁ →\n      ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ ∀ X : ℝ, 3 ≤ X →\n        ‖affineSum liouville liouville a₁ a₂ b₁ b₂ ⌊X⌋₊‖ ≤\n          C * X / Real.rpow (Real.log X) c"},{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/1"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.binary_corrected_elliott","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.lean","line":51,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"e09ff958b87d795ff14b125457531f960e91c888b12b94af672c74954f406869","statement_sha256":"sha256:97a32bf8bfa2cacc296a931f735fb2989cec00365c56a3bcf4dc1daee663d7cc","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.lean#L51"},"text":"theorem binary_corrected_elliott :\n    ∀ f₁ f₂ : ℕ → ℂ, Multiplicative f₁ → Multiplicative f₂ →\n      OneBounded f₁ → OneBounded f₂ →\n      (UniformlyNonpretentious f₁ ∨ UniformlyNonpretentious f₂) →\n      ∀ h₁ h₂ : ℕ, h₁ ≠ h₂ →\n        Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => correlationSum f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ N / (N : ℂ)) atTop (nhds 0)"},{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/2"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.affine_corrected_elliott","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.lean","line":59,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"e09ff958b87d795ff14b125457531f960e91c888b12b94af672c74954f406869","statement_sha256":"sha256:c66aa7a08afd7a2b2cec51e198f73980760f7e17d246bbf117ce1799dde95c04","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.lean#L59"},"text":"theorem affine_corrected_elliott :\n    ∀ f₁ f₂ : ℕ → ℂ, Multiplicative f₁ → Multiplicative f₂ →\n      OneBounded f₁ → OneBounded f₂ →\n      (UniformlyNonpretentious f₁ ∨ UniformlyNonpretentious f₂) →\n      ∀ a₁ a₂ b₁ b₂ : ℕ, 0 < a₁ → 0 < a₂ → a₁ * b₂ ≠ a₂ * b₁ →\n        Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => affineSum f₁ f₂ a₁ a₂ b₁ b₂ N / (N : ℂ)) atTop (nhds 0)"}],"state":"available","unresolved_names":[]},"generation_id":"sha256:fda4c3462963b650c538e2177794811eb1c221b267efea4b091fd6e397533f81","id":"l:OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations","kind":"lean-preview","omissions":[],"pairings":{"f:007":{"alternatives":[],"contributed_readings":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"content_sha256":"sha256:c5d4c35fa4e4ffa0d4129fe99e19ab550e122638357c9cebb1416fff53bb08e4","decision":"linked","detail":{"path":"lean-previews/af60b935066ded1b866aaebe.json","pointer":"/contributions/0"},"provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"review_state":"unreviewed","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.liouville_log_saving"],"general_disclaimer":false,"limitations":"This link covers only the quantitative declaration, not the other two configured conclusions.","relation":"same-claim","target":"r:Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026:thm:q-affine"},{"declarations":["OAI.OrdinaryTwoPointCorrelations.binary_corrected_elliott"],"general_disclaimer":false,"limitations":"Only the binary declaration is linked here; source correspondence is not proof verification.","relation":"same-claim","target":"r:Ordinary-two-point-correlations-of-multiplicative-functions-September-24-2026:thm:elliott"},{"declarations":["OAI.Ord